–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"37c7dcbcf0a36980d52b7d637db4e7b4f7d8c58cf962c50dc81b81ef1b0e6d75","compact":"cb6df78c85a9a17e4662bbd1cf3d5ec1c8892559b203f76af8d53dabd3155394","nasal":"4dcbdaeb5142e22265641c285e8a48396b7f9dcb97c60e5a0f9b903ba0948278"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":10,"english":"Then that hero-Dasaratha's son, Rāma, Overcome with wrath, addressed Ravana, laughing, in a harsh speech, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f9a4fc1323ffdb87b5b7ea6e0aa78138b30b1ffd61e66bbface18bfda8fb844","compact":"3dd9e5c73ca0b84caa9a87bb4d453b0e24e11f2487af6a8674d5c1a2de2aa72e","nasal":"3dd9e5c73ca0b84caa9a87bb4d453b0e24e11f2487af6a8674d5c1a2de2aa72e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":11,"english":"You vile of Räkşasas, in consequence of having through lack of sense carried off my wife from Janasthana and brought her under your subjection, you have been deprived of your prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd3d5020dbbb64477c732906dcf034b4137ca14ebd50a0c32f54d4e2637550f7","compact":"d5669fe485d20afcb3c54556dce2644ef8a598cb51cbb75d5882c2a9807c103b","nasal":"d5669fe485d20afcb3c54556dce2644ef8a598cb51cbb75d5882c2a9807c103b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":12,"english":"Having forcibly carried away Vaidehi staying in that mighty forest, forlorn and without me, you think, 'I am hero.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5ac5644729dbd76c5eba90fdf677aaa2aeb690611c051a042547dd49189a5547","compact":"10930a7a50bb3dd047110c7208149b9bc47c3198cf0f328b08fa445b2e3d38a7","nasal":"10930a7a50bb3dd047110c7208149b9bc47c3198cf0f328b08fa445b2e3d38a7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":13,"english":"Outraging the helpless wives of others, doing this craven deed, you thinkest, 'I am a hero.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"079d63e6edd484268de5bdc11d99bbcd611a6af084476baf41c8b6b676ee2538","compact":"d5aa324528b91d2782c8c8bf69d0417020d49978798448ae6378575aacd7bc77","nasal":"d5aa324528b91d2782c8c8bf69d0417020d49978798448ae6378575aacd7bc77"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":14,"english":"O you having your dignity destroyed! O shameless Wight! O you of volatile character, having through your violence brought destruction on yourself, you think, 'I am a hero.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f99f2769061de6f7f46dc18b6faab1b8f8a3b511a055d9c87f3f89acc72d54ef","compact":"0116193542a779ab167b843b45e162ad4cac107ca49915488b4481bd6c3a9daa","nasal":"308189e2cfb2ecff50398357a5e479bf3526417491da204db293f7da664d0b15"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":15,"english":"A great and famous act has been performed by you, a hero, and the brother of the Bestower of riches, surrounded with your forces!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.636,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0479e6915224c337e3f843c00e2fe573dde5ec3e972a2d7aa82c62fbfbad8f56","compact":"b272751aea4d809f06cfa270e27e3660f9758926518b10e0321f049bf5381c2e","nasal":"b272751aea4d809f06cfa270e27e3660f9758926518b10e0321f049bf5381c2e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":16,"english":"Today receive the mighty fruit of that infamous act done through pride, productive of evil.* *Remarks Rāmānuja, 'here and in the next world.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cb1ace430b8c7497d0bb469447e21713267266b3518121e58caed93fcb5d6303","compact":"53a92eb8499f850b3553d756e9fb0efb505c7930ff96c605d081f85981ae4aa7","nasal":"10b608637d92080c0ad246a010ed0a33f164782e0b9426871970525a7f6bc762"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":17,"english":"O wicked-minded one, you think of yourself, 'I am a hero; but you that have taken way Sītā like a thief, have no feeling of shame.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.78,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7c1222894e0f266fb3b96731136807be4b908acfc5043a323a2483986eb0731c","compact":"efe1ad27153990510c0c39cf8d79e9de37b14405848d2480f53ebe6573e3d03f","nasal":"efe1ad27153990510c0c39cf8d79e9de37b14405848d2480f53ebe6573e3d03f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":18,"english":"Had you forcibly outraged Sità in my very presence, you, slain by my Shafts, would have seen your brother-Khara.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f4dbf4f97b0f295e973935954305ae82abd919e2580f907e352cf800d636c3d9","compact":"3266573ddfca6e186475f501cdfcb800ddf60da4b713f59670be1d915a459247","nasal":"3266573ddfca6e186475f501cdfcb800ddf60da4b713f59670be1d915a459247"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":19,"english":"By luck, O you of an evil soul, you have come within the range of my vision. Today by means of sharp shafts shall I bring you to death's door.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.764,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d88c6bf5217ed9ad73931b7a1335b1c98e3f5a60c9f626e9701b901e8370f7ec","compact":"3917156074564156c7fe0d357597be2870877ca00002c0d2eb4543aebf679aee","nasal":"3917156074564156c7fe0d357597be2870877ca00002c0d2eb4543aebf679aee"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":20,"english":"Today beasts of pray will drag your head having burning ear-rings, severed by my shafts and covered with the dust of the battle-field.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c4125fc12ff40531fad3be411a8d457ba43c9798df1d93e0f39bc58d1c1cb1ec","compact":"17bb0cd56616445d360e6ff5c7e8fa4ff6997f23ece9d05ecb5b1c14fa7afeb0","nasal":"18889abdf980652763d9e10f20384b2e041b31fad4d4ad84d43354268d6086e6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":21,"english":"O Ravana, vultures will alight on your breast, as you will lie low on the ground; and, athirst, they will drink the blood gushing out from your wounds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.817,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ba3263b015984bf05d20df3cebea9f728574dac922820dc94ca219541bc239ef","compact":"41098207825e8bbc389e035feed1e2b8a4ec82eac4c6185fc7a63ea7bd23e24d","nasal":"6be8d31d11dc5c6c4cce673ebf44f475d816713e75a8522cd4fe609e2380d313"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":22,"english":"To-day fowls of the air will keep pulling at you pierced with my shafts, and lying lifeless, as birds do serpents.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e15d4afce3ed2b5393133b7b994e3182075d10e5160211cb1d262419cb9a64eb","compact":"5a769c5e7556848ae5117e4378a51f7ac85f718bec34a7d675d5039a88064a3e","nasal":"f33e1236df39d014a22b0ffea5d2be527a6e2b379d113ca7db4c5df1debfba14"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":23,"english":"Having spoken thus, that slayer of foes-Rāmashowered arrows on the lord of Rākşasas, staying before.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e1e4b41122dee371ff395836f231a81232ed4510f60d3cacaa26d0719a3f5479","compact":"fc5485acaa985d5f995830ac5fc15fad517da499cef26c6c00e2ad97768ce687","nasal":"3fe7689131ee43da3a798b5c8e7f9d001b7d58577b29fd874ae3f5a8f96b44f2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":24,"english":"The prowess and strength and spirits and force of arms of Rāma burning for the destruction of his foe, were doubled.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.636,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5c5e668c05c76a04b1a447eacaf50b9de2238c36105d12494c43c09543438621","compact":"90311af3f015cb0057af30e4a3cc18de08baf5c03d679039938a0eff9157ae2f","nasal":"51f88ecf988f846bad5a75cd64be1dc4ee01aa6db634ab2d31dff56af3aab6cc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":25,"english":"All the Weapons* presented themselves before that one cognisant of self; and the fleethandedness of that exceedingly powerful one increased immensely from exhilaration of spirits. *i.e. the presiding deities of them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092025","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d6796f3469d35376a8f5f8ed4b60aa364edd57bd50f75eea879df7227a955146","compact":"916a1faa25388bf47634af0962e5d267ae897c80aa086544da9363b4744902ce","nasal":"916a1faa25388bf47634af0962e5d267ae897c80aa086544da9363b4744902ce"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-26","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":26,"english":"Seeing all these auspicious omens coming of themselves, Rama, finisher of Raksasas, set about smiting his foe more energetically than ever.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd0d9365a0db34eb1700a543d80e2ca7d90b1dc24dcb2bf33e2b3dc5d8b5b80e","compact":"1bed4c73cac798d197b820b4bc508038bbe70a5205473b5fed5887e33bdcf51b","nasal":"8055a84704fff351d29e8d58fa115805c8e83170a2657da317278d16f6e41dee"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":27,"english":"Assailed with stones by the monkeys and showers of shafts by Rāghava, the Ten-necked one felt his heart undergoing a revolution.* *Vighurnahrdayah : had his heart paralysed, according to the commentator. I prefer the sense given as more graphic.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0bfc4fec6b1ea3debbf8edfdb289f868be61358d458b8056a4fd177cdee4ee84","compact":"f06c4990b729e682e71091e89bc23699f3717ba8ac38c5df8e4d375b43c96383","nasal":"f06c4990b729e682e71091e89bc23699f3717ba8ac38c5df8e4d375b43c96383"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-92-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":92,"verse":28,"english":"When through the stupefaction of his innerself, he could not discharge any weapon, or draw his bow, or put forth his prowess, (Rāma) did not persist in smiting him. And the shafts and various arms discharged by him betokened his death; and his last moments were present. And his charioteer, driving his car, perceiving this, calmly took the car away from the field of fight.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.618,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-103-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6092028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f1681fd7b49d77a6a92c6aba63224c2536edac056cfe1ebf555da5cef5dd2281","compact":"ab00879600794078032c7ef1b4caa3601342eb1ef449e3ded634a5f3bbe925fe","nasal":"52731668f520735cd8